{
  "_meta": {
    "description": "Stage 3 category keyword classifier data. Extracted from ml_service/normalization/category_classifier.py.",
    "note": "FIXED real bug: original had 'milk' in both Dairy and Beverages, and 'broccoli'/'mango'/'strawberries' in both Produce and Frozen. Dict iteration order silently picked a winner - not intentional design. Fix: 'frozen_signal_keywords' is checked FIRST by assign_category() against the RAW token (before unit/brand stripping reaches bare food name) - if a frozen-indicator word is present, category is Frozen immediately, before any other category keyword list is checked. This uses information (the raw token had 'FRZ'/'frozen' in it) that keyword-matching the bare canonical name alone can never recover. All other categories' keyword lists had their genuine duplicates removed (a term appearing in exactly one category is fine; the same term in two non-Frozen categories was still ambiguous and had to be resolved by picking the more specific category)."
  },
